From c86534742fc9d385badd515706d15ca7466db7f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 06:21:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: body pulls, path-clear targets (caves), park where we
 died twice (F-219)

- combat.kill body_pull: inch 2 yd at a time until the target alone aggroes, then back off
  `retreat` yd so it follows us out of its camp (fight log shows "body")
- runner: body_pull_spot() - the outermost mob's outer side, used when the spot where it notices
  us is outside every other camp mob's reach; parking is now the fallback (kill + clear_camp)
- kill() prefers targets whose navmesh walk passes no other hostile in aggro reach (3D - cave
  tunnels stack: Night Web Hollow pulled 5-6 spiders on the way to one)
- travel refuses a destination where we already died twice at this level and parks the quest
  (Ammen Vale's Inoculation: deaths all in defend fights, invisible to the camp rules) - not yet
  live in the running fleet

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
